spec:
  grid: 13-16 rows x 13-16 cols (square)
  background: BLACK
  blocker_colors: all 8 non-black non-blue colors (2-9) present in every input
  cell_composition:
    black: 39-56% of cells
    blue_seeds: 3-7% (5-17 pixels)
    blockers: 41-54% (colors 2-9, each 5-24 pixels)
  blue_seeds:
    mostly isolated single pixels, occasionally 2 adjacent [observed]
    most seeds have >=1 black neighbor (flood can start)
    scattered across grid, often embedded among blockers
  blockers:
    semi-random scatter with moderate clustering (avg 1.4-2.0 same-neighbor adjacency)
    form 18-35 connected components of mixed colors
    must partition black cells into >=2 disconnected regions so some black stays unreached
  unreached_black_regions:
    count: 4-20 components in output
    total unreached: 5-45 cells (3-18% of grid)
  transform:
    flood-fill 4-connected from all blue seeds through black cells
    reached black cells become blue; all other cells unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size H=W uniformly from 13-16
    2. Randomly place blocker cells (colors 2-9) covering 40-55% of grid; scatter uniformly then lightly cluster via random walks
    3. Ensure each of colors 2-9 appears at least 5 times
    4. Remaining cells are black; verify black cells form >=2 disconnected 4-connected components (reject or re-scatter if not)
    5. Pick one large black connected component as the reachable region; remaining black components become unreached (>=1 must exist with total >=4 cells)
    6. Within the reachable region, place 5-17 blue seeds (mostly isolated, scattered); each seed replaces a black cell
    7. The input is: blockers + blue seeds + all black cells (reachable + unreached)
    8. The output is: blockers + blue seeds + reachable-region black cells turned blue + unreached black cells remain black
